     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order, even with your confirmation. A 5000 mg dose three times daily delivers 15 g of acetaminophen a day. That is in the range that causes hepatotoxicity and possible liver failure, and I know of no clinical situation where it is appropriate. Confirming doesn't change that.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a standard dose.** For example, 1000 mg by mouth three times daily (3 g/day), or 1000 mg four times daily (4 g/day, the usual maximum). Give me the dose and frequency and I'll enter it.\n- **Check the intent.** If you were aiming for a particular daily total, or if this came from a unit mix-up (for example 500 mg or 5 mL), I can enter the corrected order.\n- **Escalate.** If you think the dose is justified, please discuss it with your attending and the pharmacist. They can verify it and place it through a pharmacy-reviewed process.\n\nIf this is an acetaminophen overdose or a suspected ingestion, please contact poison control and toxicology. Treatment there is N-acetylcysteine, not more acetaminophen."
      }
     ],
